1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,600
Three seconds, starting at 7.5.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:12,590
Add -c copy so it is instant.

3
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:22,120
Synthetic video. Keyframes at 0, 5, 10, 15 seconds.

4
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:28,470
Lossless, so every frame is fingerprinted.

5
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:36,450
-ss before -i: starts at 7.52 s. 75 frames.

6
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:45,320
But the file holds 138 packets. 63 are hidden pre-roll.

7
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:51,200
-ss after -i: starts at 10.00 s.

8
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:57,080
13 frames. Half a second, not three.

9
00:00:57,080 --> 00:01:03,360
Copying can only start on a keyframe.

10
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:16,830
Before -i: back to 5 s, hide the extra. After -i: forward to 10 s.

11
00:01:16,830 --> 00:01:22,770
Need exact? Re-encode.

12
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:32,660
Must copy? Check with ffprobe.

13
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:37,340
One flag moved. 75 frames or 13.

14
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:40,680
FFmpeg Reality Checks, episode 1.
